      <h2 style="color:var(--paper)">Matthew Hickey</h2>
      <p>Matthew has been a chief executive, a development director and a marketing director, and has stepped in as interim chief executive and interim marketing director when organisations needed a steady hand.</p>
      <p>He was chief executive of The Children's Literacy Charity, marketing director at the British Council, and interim marketing director at DKMS UK, where he led an integrated national campaign. At Gordon Moody, the gambling treatment charity, he was part of the leadership team that grew the organisation from £1 million to £7 million, developing new residential services and the properties to house them.</p>
      <p>He has commissioned services as well as delivered them, judged for Young Enterprise, and advised boards across the charity, gambling and financial sectors. He is a trustee of Do-it Trust and chair of a Welsh-language nursery in his home village.</p>
      <p>He holds a master's degree from Manchester Metropolitan University and a bachelor's degree from Loughborough University, and is a former elite swimmer, which may explain the interest in what it takes to keep going.</p>
      <p>Matthew lives in Llanbedrog on the Llŷn Peninsula in North Wales and works across the UK, on site and remotely.</p>
